{"l":8335,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'byrde' på engelsk?","o":["border","burglar","bundle","burden"],"a":"burden","r":"En byrde hedder 'burden'. 'Border' betyder grænse, og 'bundle' betyder bundt."},
{"l":8352,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'at blive færdig inden tiden' på engelsk?","o":["to beat the clock","to beat about the bush","to turn back the clock","to set the pace"],"a":"to beat the clock","r":"'to beat the clock' betyder at blive færdig inden tiden. Udtrykket betyder at nå noget, før tiden løber ud."},
{"l":8390,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Even the coach admitted that the other team had played better, although our team had won by one goal.' Hvad mener træneren?","o":["At de spillede bedst","At de var heldige at vinde","At kampen var kedelig","At dommeren tog fejl"],"a":"At de var heldige at vinde","r":"Træneren indrømmer, at modstanderne spillede bedre, selv om hans hold vandt."},
{"l":8420,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Sam always says he doesn't care about winning. Still, he was the last to leave training every day before the final.' Hvad antyder teksten om Sam?","o":["Han er ligeglad med finalen","Han kommer tit for sent","Han går meget op i at vinde","Han kan ikke lide at træne"],"a":"Han går meget op i at vinde","r":"'Still' viser en modsætning: han siger, han er ligeglad, men han træner mere end alle andre."},
{"l":8460,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The village has no shop, no school and only two buses a day. Yet most people who move there never want to leave.' Hvad er overraskende ved landsbyen?","o":["At landsbyen har mange busser","At der ligger en ny skole","At folk hurtigt flytter væk igen","At folk bliver boende trods manglerne"],"a":"At folk bliver boende trods manglerne","r":"'Yet' viser en kontrast: selv om der mangler meget, vil folk ikke flytte."},
{"l":8490,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The old cinema was going to be pulled down. After hundreds of local people wrote letters and organised events, the plans were changed.' Hvorfor blev planerne ændret?","o":["På grund af borgernes indsats","På grund af en ny ejer","På grund af dårligt vejr","På grund af mangel på penge"],"a":"På grund af borgernes indsats","r":"Hundredvis af lokale skrev breve og holdt arrangementer, og derefter blev planerne ændret."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'hvorved' på engelsk i 'He sold the house, ___ avoiding debt'?","o":["thereafter","thereby","whereas","hereby"],"a":"thereby","r":"'Thereby' = hvorved, på den måde."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'problem / spørgsmål' på engelsk i 'This is a serious ___'?","o":["tissue","invoice","issue","offer"],"a":"issue","r":"'Issue' betyder her et problem eller en sag."},
{"l":8500,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"B2","role":"challenge","insight":"reframing","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'uvillige' på engelsk i 'The children were ___ to go home'?","o":["eager","allowed","excited","reluctant"],"a":"reluctant","r":"'Reluctant' = uvillig."},
{"l":8520,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'You had better ___ your bike, or someone might steal it.'","o":["lock","to lock","locked","locking"],"a":"lock","r":"'Had better' efterfølges af grundformen uden 'to': 'had better lock'."},
{"l":8540,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'commence' i 'commence the ceremony'?","o":["cancel","begin","attend","record"],"a":"begin","r":"'Commence' er et formelt ord for at begynde, altså 'begin'."},
{"l":8560,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'afskaffe' på engelsk?","o":["abandon","absorb","abolish","abstain"],"a":"abolish","r":"'Abolish' betyder afskaffe, fx en lov eller en regel. 'Abandon' betyder at forlade eller opgive."},
{"l":8570,"g":8,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The organisers called the festival a modest success. Roughly half the tickets were sold, and it only rained twice.' Hvordan vurderer arrangørerne festivalen?","o":["Som en kæmpe succes for alle gæster","Som en total fiasko fra første dag","Som alt for dyr at gennemføre igen","Som nogenlunde, men ikke helt vellykket"],"a":"Som nogenlunde, men ikke helt vellykket","r":"'A modest success' betyder en beskeden succes; halvdelen af billetterne blev solgt, så det gik nogenlunde."},
{"l":8590,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'What I really need right now ___ a long holiday.'","o":["is","are","being","were"],"a":"is","r":"I en 'What'-kløvet sætning er 'What I really need' et ental-subjekt, så verbet er 'is'."},
{"l":8610,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder næsten det samme som 'lethargic' i 'feel lethargic after lunch'?","o":["anxious","sluggish","cheerful","hungry"],"a":"sluggish","r":"'Lethargic' betyder sløv og uden energi, altså 'sluggish'."},
{"l":8640,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Is it going to rain at the weekend? I hope ___.'","o":["no","don't","not","none"],"a":"not","r":"'I hope not' erstatter en hel nægtende sætning (I hope it will not rain). 'I hope no' er forkert."},
{"l":8680,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'uundværlig' på engelsk?","o":["indisputable","indistinct","independent","indispensable"],"a":"indispensable","r":"'Indispensable' betyder uundværlig. 'Indisputable' betyder ubestridelig, og 'indistinct' betyder utydelig."},
{"l":8700,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad hedder 'fordomsfri' på engelsk i 'Travelling abroad can make young people more ___.'?","o":["open-minded","absent-minded","single-minded","narrow-minded"],"a":"open-minded","r":"'Open-minded' betyder fordomsfri. 'Narrow-minded' er det modsatte, og 'absent-minded' betyder distræt."},
{"l":8720,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'meandered' i 'The river meandered slowly through the valley.'?","o":["styrtede","bugtede sig","tørrede ud","frøs til"],"a":"bugtede sig","r":"'Meander' betyder at bugte sig eller slynge sig langsomt, som en flod gennem et landskab."},
{"l":8740,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'I would rather you ___ my phone without asking.'","o":["don't use","won't use","didn't use","haven't used"],"a":"didn't use","r":"Efter 'would rather' + et andet subjekt bruges datid om nu eller fremtid: 'I would rather you didn't use'."},
{"l":8770,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'amateur' i 'an amateur photographer'?","o":["talented","young","keen","professional"],"a":"professional","r":"En 'amateur' gør noget som hobby, så det modsatte er en 'professional', der lever af det."},
{"l":8800,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The ferry is cancelled, so we ___ as well go home.'","o":["might","would","should","ought"],"a":"might","r":"'Might as well' betyder, at man lige så godt kan gøre noget, fordi der ikke er et bedre alternativ."},
{"l":8830,"g":9,"b":1,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'touch and go' i 'It was touch and go whether we would catch the last ferry.'?","o":["helt sikkert","meget usikkert","ganske ligegyldigt","meget dyrt"],"a":"meget usikkert","r":"'Touch and go' betyder, at udfaldet er meget usikkert, og at det kunne gå begge veje."},
{"l":8860,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'obscure' i 'an obscure band'?","o":["modern","unusual","famous","loud"],"a":"famous","r":"'Obscure' betyder ukendt, så det modsatte er 'famous' (berømt)."},
{"l":8900,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'If only I ___ my sister's advice before the trip!'","o":["took","have taken","would take","had taken"],"a":"had taken","r":"'If only' om fortiden kræver førnutid: 'had taken'. Det udtrykker fortrydelse."},
{"l":8920,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Preliminary data indicate a possible link between screen time and poor sleep, but researchers caution against drawing firm conclusions.' Hvad mener forskerne?","o":["At sammenhængen endnu ikke er bevist","At skærme bestemt ødelægger søvnen","At der slet ingen sammenhæng er","At man skal sove med telefonen"],"a":"At sammenhængen endnu ikke er bevist","r":"'Preliminary', 'possible link' og 'caution against drawing firm conclusions' viser, at intet er bevist endnu."},
{"l":8950,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'He talks as if he ___ the whole city, but he only moved here last month.'","o":["has known","knew","will know","had been knowing"],"a":"knew","r":"Efter 'as if' bruges datid om noget, der ikke er sandt: han kender ikke byen, men taler som om."},
{"l":8996,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'allestedsnærværende' på engelsk?","o":["ambiguous","ridiculous","ubiquitous","superfluous"],"a":"ubiquitous","r":"'Ubiquitous' betyder, at noget findes overalt."},
{"l":9000,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Only by working together ___ solve the problem.'","o":["we can","could we have","we could have","can we"],"a":"can we","r":"'Only by ...' først i sætningen kræver inversion: 'can we solve'. 'Could we have' passer ikke med grundformen 'solve'."},
{"l":9008,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'omhyggelig' på engelsk?","o":["meticulous","ridiculous","miraculous","ambitious"],"a":"meticulous","r":"'Meticulous' betyder meget omhyggelig."},
{"l":9019,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'tvetydig' på engelsk i 'The instructions were ___, so nobody knew what to do'?","o":["ambitious","ambiguous","obvious","generous"],"a":"ambiguous","r":"'Ambiguous' betyder, at noget kan forstås på flere måder."},
{"l":9028,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'splittet / tvivlrådig' på engelsk?","o":["equivalent","ambitious","ambivalent","benevolent"],"a":"ambivalent","r":"'Ambivalent' betyder at have blandede følelser."},
{"l":9040,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: '___ the instructions carefully, he started assembling the bookshelf.'","o":["Being read","Had read","To have read","Having read"],"a":"Having read","r":"'Having read' er en perfektum-participiumsætning: han læste først vejledningen og gik derefter i gang."},
{"l":9043,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'ondsindet' på engelsk?","o":["malicious","delicious","judicious","auspicious"],"a":"malicious","r":"'Malicious' = ondsindet."},
{"l":9050,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The success of the project will ___ largely on the weather.'","o":["consist","depend","insist","persist"],"a":"depend","r":"'Depend on' betyder at afhænge af. 'Consist' kræver 'of', og 'insist' og 'persist' giver ikke mening her."},
{"l":9054,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'uundgåelig' på engelsk?","o":["invisible","inedible","inevitable","irritable"],"a":"inevitable","r":"'Inevitable' betyder uundgåelig."},
{"l":9066,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'relevant' på engelsk?","o":["permanent","persistent","impertinent","pertinent"],"a":"pertinent","r":"'Pertinent' = relevant."},
{"l":9077,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'sammenhængende' på engelsk?","o":["coherent","inherent","competent","decent"],"a":"coherent","r":"'Coherent' = sammenhængende."},
{"l":9080,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Thanks so much for lending me your bike yesterday! I promise the scratch on the frame was already there. Mostly.' Hvad antyder det sidste ord?","o":["At cyklen var helt ny og uden ridser","At skribenten nok selv lavede noget af ridsen","At skribenten gerne vil købe cyklen","At ridsen allerede var blevet repareret"],"a":"At skribenten nok selv lavede noget af ridsen","r":"Ordet 'Mostly' tilføjet til sidst indrømmer halvt, at skribenten selv har lavet en del af ridsen."},
{"l":9089,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'modstridende' på engelsk?","o":["conciliatory","compulsory","contradictory","introductory"],"a":"contradictory","r":"'Contradictory' = selvmodsigende."},
{"l":9101,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'apatisk / sløv' på engelsk?","o":["pathetic","sympathetic","athletic","apathetic"],"a":"apathetic","r":"'Apathetic' = uden interesse."},
{"l":9110,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man høfligt vil sige nej til en ekstra opgave, fordi man har for travlt?","o":["I'm afraid I've got too much on right now.","I'm afraid I have too much on my head.","I'm sorry, but I am not having time.","I'm afraid I'm busy like a bee now."],"a":"I'm afraid I've got too much on right now.","r":"'I've got too much on' betyder, at man har for travlt. 'Not having time' og 'busy like a bee' er ikke korrekt engelsk."},
{"l":9112,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'streng / nøgtern' på engelsk?","o":["astute","austere","obscure","sincere"],"a":"austere","r":"'Austere' = stram, uden luksus."},
{"l":9124,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'overfladisk / letsindig' på engelsk?","o":["fabulous","furious","frivolous","ferocious"],"a":"frivolous","r":"'Frivolous' = uden alvor."},
{"l":9136,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'ildevarslende' på engelsk?","o":["anonymous","luminous","onerous","ominous"],"a":"ominous","r":"'Ominous' = ildevarslende."},
{"l":9140,"g":9,"b":2,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Not until the bell rang ___ that he had left his homework at home.'","o":["did Jonas realise","Jonas realised","realised Jonas","had Jonas realise"],"a":"did Jonas realise","r":"'Not until ...' først i sætningen kræver inversion i hovedsætningen: 'did Jonas realise'."},
{"l":9149,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'gavnlig' på engelsk?","o":["superficial","beneficial","artificial","official"],"a":"beneficial","r":"'Beneficial' betyder gavnlig."},
{"l":9159,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'indbringende' på engelsk?","o":["decorative","ludicrous","lucrative","creative"],"a":"lucrative","r":"'Lucrative' = indbringende."},
{"l":9162,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'nært forestående' på engelsk?","o":["eminent","immense","innocent","imminent"],"a":"imminent","r":"'Imminent' betyder, at noget snart sker. 'Eminent' betyder fremtrædende."},
{"l":9174,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'fremtrædende / anset' på engelsk?","o":["eminent","imminent","emergent","elegant"],"a":"eminent","r":"'Eminent' betyder fremtrædende."},
{"l":9182,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'hypotese' på engelsk?","o":["hypnosis","hypothesis","synthesis","emphasis"],"a":"hypothesis","r":"'Hypothesis' = hypotese, antagelse."},
{"l":9190,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'impeccable' i 'Her manners at the dinner were impeccable.'?","o":["upassende","gammeldags","upåklagelige","uforståelige"],"a":"upåklagelige","r":"'Impeccable' betyder fejlfri eller upåklagelig."},
{"l":9198,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'ulovlig' på engelsk?","o":["implicit","explicit","idyllic","illicit"],"a":"illicit","r":"'Illicit' betyder ulovlig."},
{"l":9205,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'svær at fange / undvigende' på engelsk?","o":["elusive","exclusive","effusive","abusive"],"a":"elusive","r":"'Elusive' = svær at få fat på."},
{"l":9217,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'nytteløs' på engelsk?","o":["fertile","futile","fragile","hostile"],"a":"futile","r":"'Futile' = nytteløs."},
{"l":9228,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'iboende' på engelsk?","o":["coherent","indolent","inherent","insolent"],"a":"inherent","r":"'Inherent' = iboende."},
{"l":9235,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'indrømme / give efter' på engelsk?","o":["conceive","conceal","convene","concede"],"a":"concede","r":"'Concede' betyder at indrømme eller opgive."},
{"l":9240,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'stringent / grundig' på engelsk?","o":["rigorous","vigorous","ridiculous","generous"],"a":"rigorous","r":"'Rigorous' = meget grundig."},
{"l":9252,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'flittig' på engelsk?","o":["delinquent","diligent","indulgent","intelligent"],"a":"diligent","r":"'Diligent' betyder flittig og omhyggelig."},
{"l":9260,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'It is high time we ___ the climate seriously.'","o":["take","will take","took","have taken"],"a":"took","r":"Efter 'It is high time' bruges datid ('took'), selv om det handler om nu: det burde allerede ske."},
{"l":9263,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'fortilfælde / præcedens' på engelsk?","o":["president","pretext","preference","precedent"],"a":"precedent","r":"'Precedent' = fortilfælde."},
{"l":9275,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'påtage sig' på engelsk?","o":["undertake","overtake","undermine","understate"],"a":"undertake","r":"'Undertake' = påtage sig."},
{"l":9287,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'vilkårlig' på engelsk?","o":["voluntary","arbitrary","sanitary","solitary"],"a":"arbitrary","r":"'Arbitrary' betyder tilfældig eller uden god grund."},
{"l":9298,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'føre tilsyn med' på engelsk?","o":["overlook","overdo","oversee","oversleep"],"a":"oversee","r":"'Oversee' = føre tilsyn med. Pas på: 'overse' hedder 'overlook'."},
{"l":9300,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The council has ___ a ban on cars in the old town centre.'","o":["opposed","exposed","composed","imposed"],"a":"imposed","r":"'Impose a ban' betyder at indføre et forbud. 'Opposed' betyder at være imod, hvilket ikke passer med 'a ban on'."},
{"l":9310,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'omgå' på engelsk?","o":["circumvent","circulate","comprehend","commemorate"],"a":"circumvent","r":"'Circumvent' = omgå (fx regler)."},
{"l":9320,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man vil sige, at noget er alt for dyrt til ens budget?","o":["It's over my money.","It's out of my price range.","It's out of my pocket.","It's beyond my wallet."],"a":"It's out of my price range.","r":"'Out of my price range' betyder, at prisen er højere end det, man har råd til. De andre vendinger er ikke faste udtryk."},
{"l":9330,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The new rules ___ a serious threat to small local shops.'","o":["set","place","pose","bring"],"a":"pose","r":"Den faste forbindelse er 'pose a threat' (udgøre en trussel)."},
{"l":9340,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad siger man på engelsk, når man fortryder noget sårende, man lige har sagt, og trækker det tilbage?","o":["I take that off.","I give that back.","I put that down.","I take that back."],"a":"I take that back.","r":"'I take that back' betyder, at man trækker sine ord tilbage. De andre er ikke faste udtryk med den betydning."},
{"l":9345,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'modvilligt' på engelsk?","o":["reluctantly","relentlessly","resolutely","repeatedly"],"a":"reluctantly","r":"'Reluctantly' betyder modvilligt."},
{"l":9356,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'offentlig granskning' på engelsk i 'The plan came under public ___'?","o":["security","scrutiny","scarcity","mutiny"],"a":"scrutiny","r":"'Scrutiny' = kritisk granskning."},
{"l":9368,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'efterspil / følgevirkninger' på engelsk?","o":["afterthought","afternoon","aftermath","aftershave"],"a":"aftermath","r":"'Aftermath' = efterspil efter en katastrofe."},
{"l":9380,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'at huske på' på engelsk?","o":["to bear a grudge","to bear fruit","to mind the gap","to bear in mind"],"a":"to bear in mind","r":"'to bear in mind' betyder at huske på. 'Bear in mind' betyder at huske på eller tage i betragtning."},
{"l":9391,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'gennembrud' på engelsk?","o":["breakthrough","breakdown","walkthrough","outbreak"],"a":"breakthrough","r":"'Breakthrough' = gennembrud."},
{"l":9400,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: '___ by the noise, the baby started to cry.'","o":["Waking","Woken","Woke","Having woken"],"a":"Woken","r":"'Woken by the noise' er en passiv participiumsætning: babyen blev vækket af larmen."},
{"l":9420,"g":9,"b":3,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'If I had studied harder last year, I ___ in the top class now.'","o":["would have been","will be","would be","had been"],"a":"would be","r":"Blandet betingelse: fortiden ('had studied') påvirker nutiden ('now'), så hovedsætningen bruger 'would be'."},
{"l":9440,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'Despite the brochure promising sea views, the only water visible from our hotel room was the swimming pool next to the car park.' Hvilken tone har teksten?","o":["Begejstret og glad","Neutral og saglig","Bange og nervøs","Skuffet og ironisk"],"a":"Skuffet og ironisk","r":"Kontrasten mellem havudsigt og en pool ved parkeringspladsen er ironisk og viser skuffelse."},
{"l":9470,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'innate' i 'an innate talent'?","o":["acquired","unusual","hidden","modest"],"a":"acquired","r":"'Innate' betyder medfødt, så det modsatte er 'acquired' (tillært)."},
{"l":9500,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'We needn't have ___ so early; the shop didn't open until ten.'","o":["leave","left","leaving","to leave"],"a":"left","r":"'Needn't have' + kort tillægsform betyder, at man gjorde noget, som viste sig at være unødvendigt."},
{"l":9550,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'jumped the gun' i 'They jumped the gun and started celebrating before the final whistle.'?","o":["sprang over hegnet","tabte modet helt","handlede for tidligt","var for langsomme"],"a":"handlede for tidligt","r":"'Jump the gun' betyder at handle for tidligt, før det rigtige tidspunkt."},
{"l":9570,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: '___ for your help, I would never have finished the project.'","o":["If it had not","Were it not been","Unless it had been","Had it not been"],"a":"Had it not been","r":"'Had it not been for' er en inverteret type 3-betingelse (= If it had not been for) og betyder 'uden din hjælp'."},
{"l":9580,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The final decision ___ with the head teacher, not with the pupils.'","o":["rests","depends","relies","counts"],"a":"rests","r":"'The decision rests with someone' betyder, at det er vedkommende, der har ansvaret for beslutningen. De andre verber kan ikke stå med 'with' her."},
{"l":9620,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'feigned' i 'He feigned illness to avoid the maths test.'?","o":["overvandt","foregav","fik","frygtede"],"a":"foregav","r":"'Feign' betyder at foregive eller simulere; han lod som om, han var syg."},
{"l":9640,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'If she weren't so shy, she ___ for the class council last week.'","o":["would run","will run","would have run","had run"],"a":"would have run","r":"Blandet betingelse: en vedvarende egenskab ('weren't so shy') påvirker fortiden ('last week'), så man bruger 'would have run'."},
{"l":9670,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The hotel advertised itself as cosy. On arrival, we discovered that this meant our room was roughly the size of a wardrobe.' Hvad mener skribenten?","o":["At værelset var meget hyggeligt","At hotellet havde store skabe","At værelset var nyistandsat","At værelset var ekstremt lille"],"a":"At værelset var ekstremt lille","r":"Skribenten afslører ironisk, at 'cosy' i reklamen dækkede over, at værelset var lille som et klædeskab."},
{"l":9690,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The decision to close the pool was met with widespread ___.'","o":["dismay","dismiss","display","disguise"],"a":"dismay","r":"'Dismay' betyder bestyrtelse eller skuffelse. De andre ord ligner, men giver ikke mening her."},
{"l":9710,"g":9,"b":4,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"l","variant":"authored","q":"Læs: 'The new shopping centre, we were told, would breathe life into the town. Five years on, half of its units stand empty.' Hvad antyder skribenten?","o":["At byen har for mange butikker","At løftet ikke er blevet indfriet","At centret blev bygget for sent","At centret er en kæmpe succes"],"a":"At løftet ikke er blevet indfriet","r":"'We were told' viser afstand til løftet, og de tomme butikker viser, at centret ikke gav byen nyt liv."},
{"l":9740,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'at stjæle opmærksomheden' på engelsk?","o":["to run the show","to steal a glance","to steal the show","to save the day"],"a":"to steal the show","r":"'to steal the show' betyder at stjæle opmærksomheden. Udtrykket betyder at være den, alle lægger mærke til."},
{"l":9760,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The proposal met with fierce ___ from local residents.'","o":["competition","ambition","condition","opposition"],"a":"opposition","r":"'Meet with fierce opposition' betyder at møde hård modstand. De andre navneord giver ikke mening her."},
{"l":9790,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'The report, ___ in 2019, still influences how schools teach climate science.'","o":["first published","first publishing","having published","was first published"],"a":"first published","r":"'First published in 2019' er en forkortet passiv participiumsætning (= which was first published). 'Was first published' ville kræve et relativt pronomen."},
{"l":9820,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'stifle' i 'She tried to stifle a yawn during the long presentation.'?","o":["efterligne","undertrykke","fremkalde","nyde"],"a":"undertrykke","r":"'Stifle' betyder at undertrykke eller kvæle, fx et gab eller et grin."},
{"l":9850,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: '___ from the top of the tower, the town looks like a model village.'","o":["Seeing","Saw","Seen","Having seen"],"a":"Seen","r":"Byen bliver set fra tårnet, så det er en passiv participiumsætning: 'Seen from the top'. 'Seeing' ville betyde, at byen selv ser."},
{"l":9880,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"h","variant":"authored","q":"Hvad betyder 'hit the ground running' i 'The new coach hit the ground running and won her first three matches.'?","o":["faldt og slog sig","startede langsomt","løb fra ansvaret","kom hurtigt godt i gang"],"a":"kom hurtigt godt i gang","r":"'Hit the ground running' betyder at gå i gang med fuld kraft og have succes fra starten."},
{"l":9890,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Hardly had the guests arrived ___ the power went out.'","o":["when","than","then","while"],"a":"when","r":"Det faste mønster er 'Hardly had ... when ...'. 'Than' hører til 'No sooner'."},
{"l":9940,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"g","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord passer: 'Were the council ___ the plan, the park would be lost.'","o":["approving","to approve","approved","approve"],"a":"to approve","r":"'Were + subjekt + to + grundform' er en formel, inverteret type 2-betingelse (= If the council approved)."},
{"l":9961,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'et utal' på engelsk i 'a ___ of options'?","o":["mirage","shortage","myriad","review"],"a":"myriad","r":"'Myriad' = utallige."},
{"l":9990,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"authored","q":"Hvilket ord betyder det modsatte af 'ascend' i 'ascend the stairs'?","o":["decorate","measure","block","descend"],"a":"descend","r":"'Ascend' betyder at stige op, så det modsatte er 'descend' (gå ned)."},
{"l":10000,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'omvendt' på engelsk?","o":["conversely","concisely","consequently","conveniently"],"a":"conversely","r":"'Conversely' = omvendt."},
{"l":10000,"g":9,"b":5,"cefr":"C1","role":"deep_challenge","insight":"perspective_shift","k":"o","variant":"reverse_meaning","q":"Hvad hedder 'være indbegrebet af' på engelsk?","o":["optimise","epitomise","economise","apologise"],"a":"epitomise","r":"'Epitomise' = være et typisk eksempel på."}
]$$::jsonb) AS e
JOIN (VALUES
  ('o', 'ordforråd', 'recall', 'factual', 'surface_association'),
  ('h', 'hverdagsudtryk', 'comprehension', 'conceptual', 'surface_association'),
  ('g', 'grammatik', 'application', 'applied', 'overgeneralization'),
  ('l', 'læseforståelse', 'analysis', 'inferential', 'surface_association')
) AS m(k, concept, skill, dtype, mis) ON m.k = e->>'k';
